From 4a40d43a8e26ee5649b68342909d55c723fa8d49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:10:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 630/630] perf(dsv41): optimize switched Engram
 lookup/sharding, decode GEMM tiles, and burst admission

1. Pass token_count=indices.shape[0] and clear_tail=False in resident Engram prepare_embeddings and share prepared_engram_hashes across resident Engram layers so decode steps launch (M, 24, 1) CTAs instead of (16384, 24, 1) CTAs and skip 201 MB tail memsets (~2.1 ms/step saved on TP6..TP8).
2. Generalize disk Engram column_shard, engram_rows_gather_kernel, and interleaved_rows to support any TP size <= 24 (including TP5 and TP7 where 24 % tp_size != 0) via padded per-rank column strides, eliminating TP5 Rank 4 4-gram skew and 6144-wide all-reduce.
3. Add TP3..TP8 decode MXFP8 GEMM tile configs in DECODE_FP8_CONFIGS and WIDE_DECODE, including tuned block_M=32 configs for (4096, 1280), (896, 15360), and WO-B (5120, 3072/2048/1024).
4. Coalesce concurrent request bursts for up to 6 ms when EngineCoreProc wakes from idle into step 0 so multi-stream bursts enter step 0 together instead of splitting 1 + (N-1).
